                <pb facs="0550" n="456" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg456"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr. Baker, chargé.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-10-14"><hi rendition="#italic">October 14,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Have Nicaragua and Salvador ratified union of June, 1895? If so, does the Diet
                    take charge of their diplomatic affairs? Minister to Guatemala telegraphs that
                    Honduras has abolished foreign office, turning over international relations to
                    Diet.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Olney.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
